    {
      "id": "claim_2848b9e137a5438ca1242092b9e3808f",
      "statement": "Filenames in an encrypted OIFS are encrypted deterministically using SIV (Synthetic IV) construction: a 24-byte synthetic nonce is derived via BLAKE2b-512 over a domain-separated context (filename_siv_key, parent_inode, plaintext_filename), then encrypted with XChaCha20-Poly1305 (filename_cipher_key) with parent_inode-bound AAD. The output is `_e_` + Base64URLUnpadded(nonce || ciphertext || 16-byte tag). Decryption verifies the SIV nonce in constant time and falls back to legacy 12-byte ChaCha20Poly1305 format for compatibility. Same filename in different directories produces unrelated ciphertexts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/encryption.rs#L634-L675",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30a56eb05b008a97b78edc44617abdcf13664bccd5b2abfb1cb905aefafc3806:"
